BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Tabletop Turnover) Tj T* () Tj T* (EXECUTIVE SUMMARY) Tj T* () Tj T* (Tabletop Turnover LLC) Tj T* () Tj T* (Problem) Tj T* () Tj T* (Independent restaurants have a big problem with the dinner rush. When the restaurant is full) Tj T* (the host do not know when the tables will be open again, so they quote wait times to guests) Tj T* (that are guesses and are often wrong. When the wait quoted is too long guests leave and go to) Tj T* (another restaurant. When the wait is too short guests get angry because they wait longer than) Tj T* (they was told. Also the host sometimes put a party of two at a table for six and then a party) Tj T* (of six have to wait even though there was a table, which is a waste of seats and revenue. This) Tj T* (problem is very painful for independent restaurants because they have thin margins, usually) Tj T* (five percent or less, and every lost table during the busiest hours of the night is lost money) Tj T* (that they can not get back. Large chains have corporate systems to deal with this but) Tj T* (independent restaurants have only paper, memory and gut feeling. We believe that this is a big) Tj T* (problem that is not solved.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Solution) Tj T* () Tj T* (Tabletop Turnover is desktop software that is installed on the computer at the host stand. The) Tj T* (software use data analytics and machine learning algorithms to predict the table turn time for) Tj T* (every table in the restaurant. It looks at the party size, the time of night, the day of the) Tj T* (week, what the guests ordered, and how long similar parties took before. Then it gives the host) Tj T* (a recommendation of which party to seat at which table and a more accurate wait time to quote) Tj T* (to the guests. The software is simple to use and has a dashboard that shows all the tables in) Tj T* (different colors. Our solution is a game changer because it takes the guessing out of the) Tj T* (dinner rush and optimizes seating to shorten waits. We chose desktop software and not a web app) Tj T* (because many independent restaurants do not have reliable internet at the host stand and they) Tj T* (want to own their data. We have built a prototype of the core prediction engine and the) Tj T* (dashboard.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Market) Tj T* () Tj T* (The restaurant industry in the United States is very large, with hundreds of billions of) Tj T* (dollars in sales every year. There are many hundreds of thousands of restaurants in the country) Tj T* (and a majority of them are independent. If just one percent of independent restaurants would) Tj T* (buy our software at our price we would have a very big business. We think our target market is) Tj T* (the full service independent restaurants with between fifteen and sixty tables that have a wait) Tj T* (during the dinner rush. These restaurants are the best fit because they are busy enough to have) Tj T* (a wait but not large enough to have a big technology budget. We have not done a formal market) Tj T* (study yet but we talked to some restaurant owners and they said the idea is interesting. The) Tj T* (market is growing because restaurants are coming back after the pandemic and more owners are) Tj T* (looking for technology to help them.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Business Model) Tj T* () Tj T* (We will charge a monthly subscription fee per restaurant. We are thinking of between fifty and) Tj T* (one hundred fifty dollars per month but we have not decided the exact price yet. We might also) Tj T* (have a setup fee for installing and connecting the software to the restaurant point of sale) Tj T* (system. In the future we could also sell extra features like reports, staff scheduling) Tj T* (suggestions and a version for restaurants with multiple locations. We could also take a small) Tj T* (percent of the extra revenue we help the restaurant make, which is another possibility. We will) Tj T* (get customers by visiting restaurants in person, by social media, by partnering with restaurant) Tj T* (associations and by word of mouth between owners. Our cost is mostly our own time, some cloud) Tj T* (servers for training the model, and some customer support. We believe our margins will be very) Tj T* (high because software is scalable and once it is built it costs little to add a new customer.) Tj T* () Tj ET
endstream
