BT /F1 10 Tf 12 TL 56 760 Td (Competition) Tj T* () Tj T* (The space of restaurant technology is crowded and there are many companies that offer) Tj T* (reservation systems, waitlist apps, point of sale systems and table management. Some of these) Tj T* (systems have some features about wait time estimates already. Many of them are well funded and) Tj T* (have big sales teams and thousands of customers. However we think we are different because we) Tj T* (are focused only on the turn time prediction and the seating optimization and because we are) Tj T* (desktop software for independent restaurants who do not want to pay for a big expensive system.) Tj T* (Our competitors are mostly trying to be everything for every restaurant while we do just one) Tj T* (thing very well. We also compete with the status quo, which is a paper chart and an experienced) Tj T* (host, and many owners think that works fine. It is possible that the big competitors could add) Tj T* (our feature easily, which is a risk we know about, but we believe our focus and our algorithm) Tj T* (will keep us ahead.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Team) Tj T* () Tj T* (Devon Kowalczyk is the chief executive officer and is a senior studying business administration) Tj T* (at our university. He worked two summers as a server and one summer as a host at a family) Tj T* (restaurant so he knows the dinner rush problem personally. He is in charge of sales, strategy) Tj T* (and customer discovery.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Marisol Yeboah-Santangelo is the chief technology officer and is a senior studying computer) Tj T* (science with a focus on data science at our university. She built the prototype and the) Tj T* (prediction model. She has experience with Python and data analysis from her classes and from a) Tj T* (research assistant job.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Preston Wuthrich is the chief operating officer and is a junior studying finance at our) Tj T* (university. He is in charge of the financial model, legal matters, and operations. He also) Tj T* (helped to register the company.) Tj T* () Tj T* (We do not yet have an advisor from the restaurant industry but we are looking for one.) Tj T* () Tj T* (Milestones and Financials) Tj T* () Tj T* (So far we have reached two milestones. First, we registered Tabletop Turnover as a limited) Tj T* (liability company. Second, we built a prototype, or minimum viable product, with a working) Tj T* (dashboard and a first version of the prediction model. The model was trained on made up data) Tj T* (that we generated ourselves and on a small sample of sales records that one restaurant owner) Tj T* (shared with us, so we still need to test it with real restaurants in real conditions. We do not) Tj T* (have paying customers or revenue yet and we do not have a website yet. We have spent a small) Tj T* (amount of our own money on legal registration and cloud costs. Our financial projection is that) Tj T* (if we get twenty restaurants in the first year paying one hundred dollars per month we would) Tj T* (have a revenue of twenty four thousand dollars, and then it will grow quickly to many more) Tj T* (restaurants in year two and year three, reaching a profit by year three. These projections are) Tj T* (estimates and they depend on many assumptions that we need to validate.) Tj T* () Tj T* (What We Ask For) Tj T* () Tj T* (We are applying to the business plan competition to get funding, mentorship and visibility for) Tj T* (our startup. If we win prize money we would use it to pay for a pilot with five to ten local) Tj T* (restaurants, to improve the prediction model with real data, to build a simple website, and to) Tj T* (pay for a part of the sales and marketing. We also would like to meet mentors who know the) Tj T* (restaurant industry and who can introduce us to restaurant owners and to investors. We believe) Tj T* (that Tabletop Turnover has the potential to be a big company that disrupt the way independent) Tj T* (restaurants manage their dinner rush, and with the help of this competition we can take the) Tj T* (next step from prototype to real customers.) Tj ET
endstream
